speechtext:
1.	For a copy of dispatches from the Secretary of State for the Colonies, dated 16th December, 1865, and 16th July, 1870, authorizing the flag of Canadian government vessels;
2.	Copy of admiralty warrant dated 2nd February, 1892, authorizing the flag of the Canadian mercantile marine "to be used on board vessels registered in the dominion";



Labour-Approval oj Convention
3.	Copy of dispatch from the Secretary of State of the Colonies, dated Downing street, 21st May, 1912, to the Governor General of Canada, in which it was stated that "the red ensign, with the arms of the Dominion of Canada in the fly, is to be used only by Canadian merchant vessels";
4.	Copy of all orders in council regulations and orders relating to aforesaid flags.
